    "text": "\u00deis spel gebyra\u00f0 seofon niht \u00e6r lenctene.\nON \u00d0YSSE WUCAN ON WODNESD\u00c6G, SWA SWA GE SYLFE WITON, is caput ieiunii, \u00fe\u00e6t is on\nWe eta\u00f0 on \u00feam sunnandagum on undern and on \u00e6fen, for\u00f0an \u00fee se sunnand\u00e6g is swa halig \u00fe\u00e6t se man\nNe eac man ne mot cneowian on sunnandagum.\nWe sculon swa \u00feeah \u00e6g\u00f0er ge on sunnondagum ge on o\u00f0rum dagum druncennysse and oferfylle\nNu ne beo\u00f0 na feowertig daga on urum lenctenlicum f\u00e6stene gefyllede, buton we f\u00e6sten \u00fe\u00e6rforan to\nOn \u00feone wodnes d\u00e6g wide geond eor\u00f0an, sacerdas bletsia\u00f0, swa swa hit geset is, cl\u00e6ne axan on cyrcan,\nNis \u00feis na ges\u00e6d be manna sawlum, ac be manna lichaman \u00fee formolsnia\u00f0 to duste, and eft sceolan on\nWe r\u00e6da\u00f0 on bocum, \u00e6g\u00f0er ge on \u00f0\u00e6re ealdan \u00e6, ge on \u00fe\u00e6re niwan, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea menn \u00fee heora synna\nNu do we \u00feis lytle on ures lenctenes anginne, \u00fe\u00e6t we streowia\u00f0 axan uppan ure heafda to geswutelunge\nSum ungerad mann w\u00e6s mid \u00c6lfstane bisceope on Wiltunscire on hirede; se man nolde gan to \u00f0am\n\u00dea b\u00e6don his geferan \u00fe\u00e6t he eode to \u00feam m\u00e6ssepreoste, and underf\u00e6ncge \u00fea gerynu \u00fee hi\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0, ic nelle.\nHi b\u00e6don \u00feagit.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he nolde, and wealode mid wordum, and s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde his wifes brucan on \u00feam\nHi leton \u00fea swa, and hit gelamp \u00fe\u00e6t se gedwola rad on \u00f0\u00e6re wucan ymbe sum \u00e6rende, \u00fea gestodon\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00f0a bebyrged, and him l\u00e6g onuppan fela byr\u00f0ena eor\u00f0an binnon seofon nihton, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e he\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re ylcan wucan com sum tru\u00f0 to \u00fe\u00e6s bisceopes hirede, se ne gymde nanes lenctenes f\u00e6stenes, ac\nHe feoll \u00fea \u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6re forman sn\u00e6de underbecc geswogen, and spaw blod; ac him gebyrede swa \u00f0eah \u00fe\u00e6t\nUs s\u00e6de eac oft A\u00feelwold, se halga bisceop \u00fee nu wyrc\u00f0 wundra \u00f0urh God, \u00fe\u00e6t he cu\u00f0e anne mann\n\u00dea sume d\u00e6g b\u00e6d he \u00feone bisceop \u00c6lfeh bl\u00e6tsian his ful.\nHe nolde, and se dysiga dranc butan bletsunge and eode him ut.\nMan sl\u00e6tte \u00fea \u00e6nne fearr feringa \u00fe\u00e6rute, and se fear arn him togeanes, and hine \u00f0yde \u00fe\u00e6t he his feorh\n\u00c6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra manna \u00fee yt o\u00f0\u00f0e drinc\u00f0 on untiman on \u00feam halgan lenctene, o\u00f0\u00f0e on rihtf\u00e6stendagum, wite\nWe sceolan gewilnian symle \u00fe\u00e6s ecean lifes, for\u00fean \u00fee on \u00feam life syndon gode dagas, na swa \u00feeah\n\u00deeah \u00fee hwa wille her on life habban gode dagas, he ne m\u00e6g hi her findan \u00feeah \u00fee he sy welig for\u00f0an\nO\u00f0\u00f0e sume o\u00f0er ungelimp on \u00feysum life him becym\u00f0, and \u00fe\u00e6rtoecean he him ondr\u00e6t his dea\u00f0es\nNe bi\u00f0 nan \u00feyssera yfela on \u00feam ecan life, ac bi\u00f0 se an goda d\u00e6g mid Gode sylfum, butan sorge and\nWel m\u00e6g gehwa witan \u00fe\u00e6t gif ahw\u00e6r is myrc\u00f0 and wuldor, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r is unasecgendlic wuldor \u00fe\u00e6r se\nWite nu \u00fe\u00e6t God ne lih\u00f0 n\u00e6fre, and warna \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu him ne leoge; gif \u00feu him lihst ne bep\u00e6cst \u00feu na hine,\nM\u00e6nig welig man is on \u00f0yssere worulde \u00fee wolde mycelne scet and ungerim feos syllan wi\u00f0 \u00feam, gif\n\u00d0eah \u00fee hit swa beon mihte \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feas blisse begitan mihte \u00fee ic nu fores\u00e6de, n\u00e6re hit swa \u00f0eah \u00fee\nNu se rica mann ne m\u00e6g her habban \u00fee ma \u00fee ure \u00e6nig \u00fea orsorgan and \u00fea unateorigendlican blysse.\nHwi nele he \u00feonne o\u00f0\u00f0e we gebycgan on \u00feysum earmum life \u00fea ecean myrh\u00f0e mid godum\nGit we magan secgan sume bysne be \u00feysum.\nGif man l\u00e6t nu \u00e6nne \u00feeof to slege hu wenst \u00f0u?\nNolde he syllan ealle his \u00e6hta \u00feeah \u00fee he welig w\u00e6re, wi\u00f0 \u00fean \u00fee he libban moste, gif man him \u00fe\u00e6s\nHe ne mihte swa\u00feeah \u00e6fre libban, \u00feeah \u00f0e he hine \u00fea ut alysde, ac he h\u00e6fde fyrst ane feawa geara.\nBi\u00f0 nu micel r\u00e6d \u00feam \u00fee his sylfes rec\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he him gebycge \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif \u00fee we embe spr\u00e6ca\u00f0.\nNu \u00feencst \u00f0u and cwi\u00f0st, hu m\u00e6g ic \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif gebycgan?\nIc \u00f0e secge, sele \u00fee sylfne Gode, swa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu lufige \u00fea \u00f0ingc \u00fee God lufa\u00f0, and \u00fea \u00f0incg onscunie \u00fee\nGod ascuna\u00f0 leasunga and lufa\u00f0 so\u00f0f\u00e6stnysse.\nNe beo \u00feu na leasbreda o\u00fe\u00fee swicol, ac beo so\u00f0f\u00e6st and symle getrywe, for\u00f0an \u00fee se trywleasa ne bi\u00f0\nHit bi\u00f0 swi\u00f0e langsum \u00fe\u00e6t we ealle godes beboda her nu eow gereccan, ac do\u00f0 an \u00f0incg; cepe gehwa\nGif he hw\u00e6t tobrece ongean Godes willan bete \u00fe\u00e6t georne, \u00feonne bi\u00f0 he Godes mann and God him\nNu bi\u00f0 \u00e6lc mann gefullod on naman \u00fe\u00e6re halgan \u00ferynnysse, and he ne mot na beon eft gefullod, \u00fe\u00e6t\nSe mildheorta God cw\u00e6\u00f0 be eallum synfullum mannum twa word swi\u00f0e fremfulle, Declina a malo et\nNis genoh \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu fram yfele buge, butan \u00feu symle be \u00feinre m\u00e6\u00f0e god gefremme.\nD\u00e6dbot mid geswicennysse yfeles, and \u00e6lmysd\u00e6da, and halige gebedu, and geleafa, and hiht on\nGod cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he nolde \u00fe\u00e6s synfullan dea\u00f0, ac he wile swy\u00f0or \u00fe\u00e6t he gecyrre fram his synnum and\nEft cw\u00e6\u00f0 se \u00e6lmihtiga God, Gif se arleasa and se synfulla wyrc\u00f0 d\u00e6dbote ealra his synna, and hylt\nNis nan leahter swa healic \u00fe\u00e6t man ne m\u00e6g gebetan, gif he yfeles geswyc\u00f0, and mid so\u00f0re\nSe man \u00fee wile his synna bewepan, and wi\u00f0 god gebetan \u00feonne mot he geornlice warnian, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6ft\nSe man \u00fee \u00e6fter his d\u00e6dbote his manfullan d\u00e6da geedniwa\u00f0, se gegrema\u00f0 God, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he bi\u00f0 \u00feam\nNe nan man ne sceal elcian \u00fe\u00e6t he his synna gebete, for\u00f0an \u00fee God behet \u00e6lcum behreowsigendum\nNe sceamige nanum menn \u00fe\u00e6t he anum lareowe his gyltas cy\u00f0e, for\u00f0an \u00fee se \u00fee nele his synna on\n\u00de\u00e6r beo\u00f0 cu\u00f0e ure ealra d\u00e6da eallum \u00feam werodum, and se\u00f0e ne m\u00e6g for sceame his gyltas anum\nWitodlice ne begit nan mann hys synna forgifnysse \u00e6t Gode, buton he hi sumum Godes menn\nEft ne mot nan mann ne ne sceal secgan on hine sylfne \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e he wyrcende n\u00e6s, swa swa we on\nHieronimus se halga lareow awrat on sumere stowe be \u00f0am wife \u00feus; He cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t sum wer w\u00e6re \u00fee\nHi wurdon \u00fea beswungene and swy\u00f0lice getintregode, swa swa \u00fea w\u00e6s gewunelic to witnigenne\nHi man clifrode \u00fea mid isenum clawum, \u00fe\u00e6t hi sceoldan secgan hwe\u00f0er hit so\u00f0 w\u00e6re.\n\u00d0a wolde se cniht his wite geendian mid sceortum dea\u00f0e, and fors\u00e6de hi buta.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t anr\u00e6de wif betwux \u00feam an\u00f0r\u00e6cum witum, Eala \u00f0u Drihten Crist, \u00fee ealle digle \u00feincg\nHeo cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to \u00f0am cnihte, eala \u00feu forcu\u00f0ost manna.\nHwi woldest \u00feu forsecgan unc unscildige swa?\nIc wylle eac sweltan na scyldig swa\u00feeah, and ic ferige mid me for\u00f0 unsce\u00f0\u00feignysse, for\u00f0an \u00fee\n\u00dea wundrode se dema \u00fe\u00e6s wifes anr\u00e6dnysse, \u00fe\u00e6t heo nolde andettan on swa earfo\u00feum witum, \u00fe\u00e6t se\n\u00dea arn \u00fe\u00e6t folc to ardlice for wafunge, and se cwellere sloh sona \u00feone cniht \u00fee hine sylfne forleah, \u00fe\u00e6t\nHeo let to slege and he sloh \u00fea to mid eallum m\u00e6gene, ac \u00fe\u00e6t swurd ne mihte buton \u00fea hyde ceorfan,\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea ofsceamod and sloh eft swi\u00f0e.\n\u00dea \u00e6tstod \u00fe\u00e6t swurd and \u00feone swuran ne hrepode, ac \u00feam cwellere \u00e6tfeoll f\u00e6rlice his gold, \u00fea\u00fea he\n\u00de\u00e6t wif him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Cniht nim \u00fein gold, \u00fee l\u00e6s \u00fee hit \u00fee losige \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u lange beswunce.\nSwa orsorh w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t wif under \u00feam w\u00e6lhreowan cwellere, \u00fe\u00e6t heo locode his goldes \u00fee hi belifian vel\n\u00dea sloh se cwellere git mid \u00feam swurde hire to, ac seo halige \u00ferynnys \u00fe\u00e6t swurd gelette, \u00fe\u00e6t hit\n\u00dea wolde he \u00feurh\u00feyn hi \u00fewyres mid \u00feam swurde, ac se ord bigde upp to \u00feam hiltum, and ne dorste hi\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 eall seo meniu \u00fee \u00f0\u00e6r mid stod ofwundrod, \u00fe\u00e6t se cwellere ne sceolde swencan hi na leng,\nGod wolde \u00fea git his wundra geswutelian \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t anr\u00e6de wif, and him gewear\u00f0 \u00fea eallum \u00fe\u00e6t man\nHeo wear\u00f0 \u00fea ofslagan, ac hire swura n\u00e6s \u00feurhslagen.\nHeo w\u00e6s swa\u00feeah dead and sona bebyrged, ac God hi eft ar\u00e6rde ea\u00f0elice of dea\u00f0e on \u00fe\u00e6re ylcan\nHeo nolde seccgan unso\u00f0 and hi sylfe fordeman, for\u00f0an \u00fee se leasa mu\u00f0 ofslih\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s mannes sawle.\nNu ge habba\u00f0 gehyred \u00fe\u00e6t ge forhelan ne sceolan eowre agenne synne ne eac secgan na mare \u00feonne\nSe cniht leah on hine sylfne and ofslagen wear\u00f0 sona, swa eac Dauid cynincg het acwellan \u00feone mann\nDauid clypode \u00fea\u00f0a se cniht dead w\u00e6s, Nu \u00f0u cw\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu acwealdest \u00feone cynincg Saul, beo \u00fein\nSe man \u00fee wile his synna andettan and gebetan, he sceal don \u00feonne forgifnysse eallum \u00feam mannum\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0, Buton ge forgifan \u00feam mannum \u00fee wi\u00f0 eow agylta\u00f0 mid inwerdre heortan, nele se\n\u00c6lc Cristen man sceal cunnan his paternoster and his credan.\nMid \u00feam paternostre he sceal hine gebiddan, and mid \u00feam credan he sceal his geleafan getrymman.\nSe lareow sceal secgan \u00feam l\u00e6wedum mannum \u00fe\u00e6t andgyt to \u00feam paternostre and to \u00f0am credan, \u00fe\u00e6t\nWe sceolan beon \u00feeonde symble on godnysse, and elce d\u00e6g geeacnian us \u00fea ecean speda \u00fea hwile \u00fee\nNe sceal nan mann wenan ne on his mode \u00feencan \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6bbe gefremod fela to gode, and ne \u00feurfe\nFela halige menn fram frym\u00f0e middaneardes w\u00e6ron beforan us wundorlice ge\u00feogene, \u00feam we nu\nEft is us to smeagenne hu se \u00e6lmihtiga Crist his eadmodnysse cydde, \u00fea\u00f0a he to cwale sealde hine\nHu m\u00e6g nu manna eadmodnys beon mycel ge\u00feuht, togeanes his eadmodnysse \u00fee \u00e6lmihtig God is.\nWe s\u00e6don nu \u00feis spel, for\u00f0an \u00fee her bi\u00f0 l\u00e6s manna on wodnes d\u00e6g, \u00f0onne nu to d\u00e6g beo\u00f0, and eow\nSy him a wuldor \u00f0e leofa\u00f0 and rixa\u00f0 on ecnysse, ece drihten; AMen.",
